  That project carries achan1989/ghidra-65816 near-verbatim (a direct diff of the
  two 658xx.sinc files shows only whitespace and one comment typo), so the
  copyright above names both lineages; see its CREDITS.md.

  This is a fork point, not a re-sync target: bead grm-9nxj.2 changes how
  immediate operands are represented, since upstream models them as references
  dereferenced out of the instruction stream, which defeats the constant
  propagation this project's bank-value recovery depends on. Vendored verbatim
  at the commit above; the only modification is a prepended attribution header.

  Not vendored, and written for this project instead: w65816.slaspec,
  w65816.ldefs (language id 65816:LE:24:retro, so it cannot collide with
  upstream's 65816:LE:24:snes) and w65816.pspec, which adds the emulation-mode
  context defaults upstream omits and deliberately drops upstream's SNES
  register symbols -- IO naming here comes from the machine descriptor, not the
  language. Upstream's SNES ROM loader and .opinion file are not vendored.
